+## Deploy
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=mhyfritz%2Fastro-landing-page)
+
+Wasmer detects this as a static Astro site: it runs `npm install` and `npm run build` and serves the generated `dist/` folder. The button opens Wasmer's import page for this public repository, where you review the detected settings (and correct the preset or build settings if needed) before clicking Deploy; nothing is deployed until you do. It does not create a copy of the repository in your GitHub account; to customize the site, fork the repository and import your fork instead.
